CHAPTER.VERS:
Sing to God, sing praises to his name: Cast up a highway for him who rides through the deserts; His name is Yah; and exult

          {+}
         before him.

When you

          {+}
         lie among the sheepfolds, [It is as] the wings of a dove covered with silver, And her pinions with yellow gold.

Why do you

          {+}
         look askance, you

          {+}
         high mountains, At the mountain which God has desired for his dwelling place? Yes, Yahweh will stay [in it] forever.

Bless

          {+}
         God in the congregations, Even the Lord, [you

          {+}
         who are] of the fountain of Israel.

Sing to God, you

          {+}
         kingdoms of the earth; Oh sing praises to the Lord; Selah.

Ascribe

          {+}
         strength to God: His excellency is over Israel, And his strength is in the skies.
